-# S002 Review and confirm
+# Story: Review and confirm proposed actions
 
-TODO
+**Story ID**: `S002-review-confirm` &nbsp;·&nbsp; **Qualified**: `E001/S002`
+**Created**: 2026-08-10
+**Status**: Specified
+**Input**: S001 uploads and extracts proposals; S002 reviews and confirms them; S003 schedules confirmed actions.
+
+**Current State**: Specified
+- [x] **Draft**
+- [x] **Specified**
+
+---
+
+## 1. Experience (What the user lives)
+
+### 1a. JTBD Context
+
+**When** S001 has produced proposed actions from an uploaded item, the reviewer wants to inspect those proposals and explicitly confirm the ones that are ready, **so that** only human-approved actions move forward to scheduling.
+
+No `product-contract.md` is present in this workspace, so this story makes no magic-moment claim (`serves: []`).
+
+### 1b. Primary User Story
+
+As a reviewer, I want to review proposed actions and confirm the appropriate ones so that later scheduling acts only on items I have approved.
+
+### 1c. Felt Quality (How the user feels)
+
+| Surface | Entry emotional state | Target felt outcome | Banned feelings |
+|---------|----------------------|--------------------|-----------------|
+| Proposed-action review | Cautious about acting on an extracted proposal | In control because each action is visibly reviewed before confirmation | Pressure, ambiguity, accidental commitment |
+| Confirmation result | Ready to proceed after deciding | Certain that the selected action is approved and can advance | Doubt, hidden state, repeated work |
+| Empty/unavailable proposals | Waiting for S001 output or with nothing to approve | Clearly informed that there is nothing available to confirm | Confusion, a misleading success state |
+
+### 1d. Magic Moments Tied to This Story
+
+No magic moments can be tied without a `product-contract.md`; the story deliberately claims none in `serves:`.
+
+## 2. Acceptance LARP (How we prove the experience works)
+
+### 2a. Required Personas to LARP
+
+| Persona | Flow | Build artifact | Evidence required |
+|---------|------|----------------|-------------------|
+| reviewer | Review proposals created by S001, confirm a selected proposal, and observe its confirmed state | Running review surface | Screenshot, accessible interaction record, and LARP findings |
+
+### 2b. Acceptance Scenarios
+
+#### AC-1 — Review available proposals
+- **GIVEN** the running build has one or more proposals produced by S001 that have not yet been confirmed
+- **WHEN** the reviewer opens the review surface
+- **THEN** each available proposal can be inspected before the reviewer confirms it
+- **AND** the surface distinguishes proposals awaiting review from any confirmed proposal
+- **EVIDENCE** screenshot of the review surface and an accessibility-tree or interaction transcript showing the available proposals
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-2 — Confirm an intended proposal
+- **GIVEN** the reviewer is viewing an available proposal from S001
+- **WHEN** the reviewer confirms that proposal
+- **THEN** the proposal visibly becomes confirmed
+- **AND** the confirmation is scoped to the proposal the reviewer selected, leaving other available proposals unconfirmed
+- **EVIDENCE** before-and-after screenshots and an interaction transcript identifying the selected proposal and its confirmed state
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-3 — Do not imply confirmation when nothing is available
+- **GIVEN** the running build has no proposal from S001 available for review
+- **WHEN** the reviewer opens the review surface or attempts to confirm
+- **THEN** the surface clearly communicates that no proposal can be confirmed
+- **AND** it does not present an unavailable proposal as confirmed
+- **EVIDENCE** screenshot and accessibility-tree or interaction transcript of the unavailable state
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+## 3. Evidence Required
+
+No `evidence-contract.md` is present; these are story-local requirements to be reconciled when that project artifact exists.
+
+| Evidence type | Required for state | Verifiable by | Path / convention |
+|---------------|--------------------|---------------|-------------------|
+| Review-surface screenshot | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `screenshots/<sha>-review.png` |
+| Confirmation result screenshot | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `screenshots/<sha>-confirmed.png` |
+| Accessible interaction record | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `larp-recordings/<sha>-reviewer.md` |
+| Persona LARP findings | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `larp-recordings/<sha>-reviewer-findings.md` |
+| Adversarial probe results | SHIP-RC | agent-LARP | `audit-report.md` |
+
+## 4. Adversarial Cases (What must NOT happen)
+
+| Condition | Must NOT happen | Probe used to verify |
+|-----------|-----------------|----------------------|
+| A reviewer selects one proposal | A different proposal is marked confirmed | Confirm a uniquely labelled proposal while another remains available; inspect both states |
+| No proposals are available | The surface displays an invented proposal or a success state | Open and attempt the confirmation flow with an empty proposal set |
+| A proposal is already confirmed | A repeated interaction silently makes its state ambiguous | Reopen the review surface after confirmation and inspect the displayed state |
+| Review data cannot be loaded | The surface claims confirmation occurred | Simulate unavailable review data and inspect the visible outcome |
+
+## 5. Failure-Modes Handled
+
+| Dependency | Failure mode | Behavior | Verified by |
+|------------|--------------|----------|-------------|
+| S001 proposal output | No proposal is available | The reviewer sees a clear unavailable state and cannot mistake it for confirmation | AC-3 LARP |
+| Proposal state source | Review data cannot be loaded | The surface does not report a proposal as confirmed without visible support | Adversarial unavailable-data probe |
+| Confirmation state update | The selected proposal cannot be recorded as confirmed | The reviewer is not shown a confirmed result for that proposal | Adversarial state-update probe |
+
+## 6. Related Tables / Surfaces (Cascade)
+
+| Write target | Related tables | Cascade behavior | Verified |
+|--------------|----------------|-------------------|----------|
+| Proposed action confirmation state | Review surface and the scheduling input consumed by S003 | Only the selected proposal advances as confirmed; unconfirmed proposals remain reviewable | AC-2 LARP |
+
+## 7. Performance + Non-Functional Targets
+
+- Performance: The confirmation result is visible within the same review flow; no numeric project target is available in the workspace.
+- Accessibility: The available, confirmed, and unavailable states are distinguishable in the review surface and its accessibility record.
+- Security/privacy: Confirmation requires an explicit reviewer action; no additional policy is available in this workspace.
+- Observability: The LARP record identifies the selected proposal and observed post-confirmation state.
+
+## 8. Data + API (Last, not first)
+
+### Key Entities
+- **Proposed action**: An action candidate produced by S001 that is awaiting human review.
+- **Confirmed action**: A proposed action that a reviewer has explicitly approved for S003 to schedule.
+
+### API Surface
+
+No API contract is specified at this phase. The later technical plan must select the mechanism that reads proposals and records confirmation.
+
+## 9. Implementation Hint (Optional)
+
+Keep confirmation explicit and proposal-specific. Technical design is intentionally deferred to `plan.md`.
+
